            <ArticleTitle>Mode of delivery and risk of developing allergic disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>800-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this study was to quantify the relationship between mode of delivery and subsequent incidence of allergic disease. The analysis is based on data derived from a birth cohort of 24,690 children who contributed data to the West Midlands General Practice Research Database. We found no convincing evidence to suggest that babies born by caesarean, forceps, or breech delivery had an increased risk of developing allergic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
